Dan Royer <aggrav8d@hotmail.com> deserves a cookie for saying:
> Now I don't go running if my health is low,

I'm not sure what you mean.  You _should_ go running if your health is
low.  

> and I've do my best to hang on to sensible things like scroll of
> teleport so i can escape a tricky situation.  In spite of this I have
> never been able to pass level 9xp.  My luck can NOT be this bad.  One
> time I am swarmed by killer bees,

If a swarm of killer bees kills you, that's not bad luck, it's poor
planning.  You were too far away from the stairs and/or didn't have
proper means of escape.  

Bees (and ants) are barely faster than you, since you start with speed,
so unless you backed yourself into a corner, you should almost always be
able to escape.

> twice I read scrolls that teleported me down 4 floors right next to
> something with a touch of death (maybe) or a mindflayer... 

No mindflayers or high-level spellcasters will be randomly generated on
the levels that you've reached, so don't bother worrying too much about
them.  If you end up next to one after a teleport, it's a fluke.
However, they can still be beaten with such things as creative
engraving.  ;)  Or, you can just escape again.

> Note that by this time I've almost always lost my dog, he either gets
> killed or starves (which is stupid, there's enough corpses lying
> around)

It's very hard for your pet to starve in a normal game.  As you said,
there are plenty of corpses around.  They'll also happily eat tripe
rations, food rations, etc...  How exactly is your pet not getting to
these corpses and food items?  

> Also note that I never seem to have enough food.  I've died from
> fainting in a fight more times that I care to recall - I eat the
> corpses I know aren't poisoned (such as bats) and I buy all the
> tripes, fruit, and guyokis I can when I'm in a shop. 

Fruit isn't worth it.  Tripe isn't worth it for anything but a pet.
Randomly generated food, shops, and prayer should be enough to keep 99%
of characters from starving.  I suspect you're ignoring the latter.

> I have reached the zoo at the end of sokoban (once) but which
> carefully picking off creatures a group of urukhai came up behind me
> and one of them had a wand of magic missile.

So, get out of his line of sight.  Both top levels of sokoban provide
ample architecture to hide behind.  That should make the wand a
non-issue.  If you still get killed, I suspect your AC was way too high,
you had a poor weapon, and/or your XL wasn't high enough.  And you
didn't bring enough healing/escape items.  

